      "id": "hackernews-2026-07-08-list-of-european-organizations-that-have-banned-personal-mes",
      "title": "List of European organizations that have banned personal messaging apps at work",
      "summary": "Article URL: https://www.birdy.chat/blog/the-growing-list-of-european-organisations-that-ban-personal-messaging-apps-at-work\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48830371\nPoints: 34\n# Comments: 36",
      "body": "If using personal messaging apps for work has ever felt a bit wrong to you, you're not alone. In surveys, around seven out of ten office workers¹ say they share work information over these apps. And many of us have had the same quiet question while typing: should this conversation really happen here?That feeling makes sense. The real risks come down to two things: control over the channel, and a record of your conversations (a \"paper trail\") when your organisation needs one. On a personal app, your organisation cannot decide what is kept and what is deleted. It cannot control who is part of a conversation. And it cannot show last year's messages when a regulator, a court, or a customer dispute requires them. A growing number of European organisations have understood this and acted on it. What started as a data-protection question in German industry has become, year by year, a question of record-keeping, compliance, and digital sovereignty across Europe. We have collected the cases below and the list covers both formal bans and formal restrictions. We plan to keep this list up to date. If you know an organisation that belongs on it, send us a message (hello@birdy.chat) and we will add it to the list.Productively yours,Rolands",
      "source": "Hacker News",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [],
      "author": "rmesters",
      "publishedAt": "2026-07-08T11:03:34.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://framerusercontent.com/assets/Oseve1wSn29K7t4kaok0Gm0PU78.jpg",
      "originalUrl": "https://www.birdy.chat/blog/the-growing-list-of-european-organisations-that-ban-personal-messaging-apps-at-work",
      "readTimeMinutes": 1,
      "language": "en"
