      "id": "hackernews-2026-07-07-amazon-without-the-knockoffs",
      "title": "Amazon without the knockoffs",
      "summary": "Article URL: https://knockoff.shopping/\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48818963\nPoints: 249\n# Comments: 170",
      "body": "Knockoff filters the trademark-squat pseudo-brands (the SZHLUXes and\nHORUSDYs) out of your search results, so what's left is brands with a reputation to lose.\nFree, fair source (FSL), no accounts, no tracking. Works on every Amazon marketplace.\nWNPETHOME XL Extra Large Dog Bed, Washable Dog CouchOn the pseudo-brand list\nCasper Dog Bed, Plush Memory Foam, Large, SandEstablished brand\nEHEYCIGA Orthopedic Dog Beds for Extra Large DogsOn the pseudo-brand list\nCarhartt Durable Canvas Pet Bed, Water Resistant DuckEstablished brand\nJunk gets flagged, dimmed, or hidden. Your call. Real brands pass untouched.\nHow it worksEvery listing, appraised in place.\nNo accounts, no cloud lookups on your shopping path. The whole appraisal\nruns locally in your browser, on every Amazon page you open.\n1Checked against 5,000+ real brands\nA bundled register of established brands, including the community-maintained\nAmazonBrandFilterList, refreshed daily. Real brands pass instantly.\nPseudo-brands have a linguistic signature: ALL-CAPS squat-length strings, vanishing\nvowels, unpronounceable consonant runs. Knockoff scores every unknown name against it.\nRelaxed, Standard, or Strict, and flagged items are hidden, dimmed, or just labeled.\nEvery verdict is one click from being overridden.\nFeaturesBuilt like a tool, not a toy.\nFiltered listings can vanish entirely (with a one-click reveal), fade until hovered, or just wear a warning chip.\nFlip one toggle to strip Amazon's paid “Sponsored” listings out of search, too. Off by default. Your call.\nTrust or block any brand from the results page. Your personal lists override every other signal, always.\nRelaxed catches the notorious offenders. Standard adds suspect names and unbranded listings. Strict allows only recognized brands.\nOne-click misclassification reports feed a curated list that reaches every install within a day, no update required.\nNo accounts, no analytics, no tracking. The only network request is a daily brand-list refresh. Reports are opt-in and anonymous.\nFSL-1.1-MIT, converting to MIT after two years. No build step, readable in an afternoon. The brand lists are plain text files, so fixing a misclassification is a one-line PR.\nFair sourceHelp draw the line.\nThe junk-brand arms race is only winnable together. Add brands, tune the heuristics,\nor just report misclassifications from inside the extension. Every fix ships to everyone.",
      "source": "Hacker News",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [],
      "author": "plurby",
      "publishedAt": "2026-07-07T15:13:01.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://knockoff.shopping/og.png",
