      "id": "hackernews-2026-07-05-delta-flight-hit-by-firework-while-landing-at-midway-airport",
      "title": "Delta flight hit by firework while landing at Midway Airport on Fourth of July",
      "summary": "Article URL: https://www.nbcchicago.com/news/local/delta-flight-hit-by-firework-while-landing-at-midway-airport-on-fourth-of-july/3957451/\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48797141\nPoints: 126\n# Comments: 223",
      "body": "The aircraft landed safely, and the incident didn't result in an emergency landing, airline officials said.\nAn investigation was underway after a Delta flight landing at Midway Airport was hit by a firework on the Fourth of July.\nA Delta flight arriving at Chicago's Midway International Airport on the Fourth of July reportedly made contact with a firework, the airline said.\nDelta Air Lines Flight 1076 departed Hartsfield-Jackson International Airport at 7:36 p.m. ET and landed at Midway Airport at 8:38 p.m. CT, according to the flight-tracking website FlightAware.com.\nRadio communication between the cabin crew and air traffic control captured the moments after the incident.\n“Tower, we just had a firework hit our plane, Delta 1076, we're continuing,\" air traffic control audio revealed. \"We just heard a bang on the plane, so we'll have to look at it when we get to the gate. We're just hoping it was just a mortar that went off underneath, but definitely felt a big bang.”\nThe aircraft landed safely, and the incident didn't result in an emergency landing, airline officials said.\nDelta said Sunday a post-flight inspection showed no damage to the aircraft.\nThe Federal Aviation Administration is investigating.",
