      "title": "Tech Now",
      "summary": "Adrienne Murray meets the team using technology to preserve a historic warship in Sweden.",
      "body": "Home            News            Sport            Weather            iPlayer            Sounds            Bitesize     CBeebies     CBBC     Food         Home     News     Sport     Business     Technology     Health     Culture     Arts     Travel     Earth     Audio     Video     Live             Home            News            Sport            Weather            iPlayer            Sounds            Bitesize     CBeebies     CBBC     Food        Home     News     Sport     Business     Technology     Health     Culture     Arts     Travel     Earth     Audio     Video     Live         Close menu\nFIFA World CupA-ZTV GuideWatchlistHomeTech NowSaving a ShipwreckTech Now - Saving a ShipwreckAdrienne Murray meets the team using technology to preserve a historic warship in Sweden. Shiona McCallum has a round-up of the key innovations and trends on show at VivaTech in Paris. Duration25 minsFirst shown4 Jul 2026Available for 11 monthsAudio DescribedSign LanguageEpisodes EpisodesThis episodeWorld Cup: Game-Changing TechShiona McCallum visits Fifa HQ in Zurich to see new tech being used in the World Cup.Shiona McCallum meets a medical expert testing out the future of prosthetics.Adrienne Murray explores how new 3D imaging is supporting heart procedures.Deep Dive: Underwater TechAndrew Rogers explores new tech trials helping people stay underwater for longer.Art Mystery: Can AI Solve It? Harriet Bradshaw finds out how AI is being used to help solve an art history mystery. Blenheim Palace: Can Tech Help to Restore it?Shiona McCallum tours Blenheim Palace, exploring the tech aiding its restoration.Climate Science in the CourtroomHow research linking climate change and extreme weather events is being used in lawsuits.Inside the High-Tech Insect FarmAlasdair Keane visits the underground insect farm turning food waste into animal feed.MWC Barcelona: What's New In Phone Tech?Paul Carter checks out the newest phones, gadgets and trends from MWC Barcelona. Norway's Fjords: Can Tourism Go Green?Alasdair Keane climbs aboard an electric boat in Norway.Inside Europe’s Space RaceAdrienne Murray visits the Esrange Spaceport in the extreme north of Sweden.Winter Olympics: Can Tech Boost Performance?Alasdair Keane visits the Olympic training centre in Oslo.Future Farming in AustraliaNick Kwek meets innovators using tech for Australia's agricultural industry.From Las Vegas, the latest trends and innovations at CES 2026.Jacqui Wakefield joins singer KT Tunstall as she sees her musical avatar.Space Exploration: Can Robots Lead the Way?Nick Kwek visits the National Space Industry Hub in Sydney.Icebreaker Tech: Navigating the ArcticAdrienne Murray meets the engineers designing icebreaker ship technology for the Arctic.Rising Seas: Can Tech Help Us Prepare?The scientists on a quest to improve our predictions of global sea level rise.Fixing Fashion's Sizing ProblemShiona McCallum meets an AI startup working to fix erratic clothing sizes in fashion.Movie Tech: Behind the ScenesAlasdair Keane explores a high-tech studio that transforms how car stunts are made.Brain Cells and BiocomputingZoe Kleinman meets the scientists trying to make living computers using brain cells.Cloud Seeding and Conspiracy TheoriesMarco Silva unpacks the science and technology of cloud seeding.IFA Berlin: The Rise of Smart TechAlasdair Keane explores the tech highlights at IFA Berlin.Lara Lewington explores the tech being trialled to find 'hidden' pancreatic cancer cases.Fighting Wildfires: Can Tech Help?How technology is bringing hope of earlier detection and prevention to wildfires.AI and the Future of HumanityJoe Tidy explores how the rise of artificial intelligence may play out.Sagrada Família: Can Tech Help Complete It?Yasmin Morgan-Griffiths has exclusive access to La Sagrada Familia in Barcelona.Lithium Mining: The ImpactIone Wells explores if lithium mining can be done more sustainably.Exploring some of the latest tech innovations in the world of sport.",
